// The journal's lab: the Moth, her journal worn on her wrist and her companion, on the basis's floor under a clear day,
// booted alone so a change to the journal, its wrist panel, its pages, the menagerie or a companion's creation bakes and
// settles in a fraction of the debug world's time (AGENTS.md, the labs ruling). Boot it with
// `--world worlds/debug/labs/journal.puck`; the seat starts on the stage.
//
// What it holds, and nothing else:
//
//   - the Moth (../avatars/moth/moth.puck), whose stage basis brings her journal (../../standard/journal.puck), its wrist panel on
//     her gauntlets (../../standard/wrist-panel.puck) and her menagerie (../../standard/menagerie.puck, with
//     ../menagerie.puck's kinds), so she starts keeping Mintstitch and Tangerine with Mintstitch active;
//   - her companion (../../standard/companion.puck), wearing whichever kind is active.
//
// To work it: I opens the journal and closes it (the View page's West on a pad), so does Backspace while it is open.
// Standing still she raises her left forearm and the camera focuses in (the pause read); walking, she glances at it (the
// action read). The arrows' up and down mark a companion on the menagerie page, Enter calls it, and the companion
// changes to it; the arrows' left and right turn to the quest, marks and notes pages. `journal.hand.right` moves the
// panel to her right forearm, `journal.hand.left` back.
//
// The portal hook is the id `journal`. The gallery's lab wing connects it with one painting row named `journal` whose
// destination is the reference `journal` (this document), and a crossing arrives at the spawn point `journal`, a few
// steps from the stage facing it.

schema: "puck.world.definition.v1"
basis: "../stage"
documentId: "journal"

import "../set-controls"
import "../../standard/skies"
import "../../standard/companion"

metadata {
  title: "Journal lab"
  description: "The Moth's journal worn on her wrist, its menagerie page and her companion, on a small floor."
}

// The hook's arrival, facing the stage.
spawnPoints [
  { id: "journal", position [0, 0, 4], yawDegrees: 180 }
]

// The companion inhabits the population's top slot, the only inhabitant here.
let journalLabCompanionBody = 7

companionDesign(population: 8)
companion(owner: 0, slot: journalLabCompanionBody, position: [-1.2, 1.52, 1], menagerie: true)

render {
  farDistance: 200
  lighting {
    lights [
      sunlight(direction: [-2, 4, -3], color: "#FFF1D6", illuminance: 60000lx)
    ]
  }
  sky {
    clearDay()
  }
  atmosphere {
    clearDayAir()
  }
}
